        <type>int64_t</type>
        <definition>int64_t vy_read_view::vlsn</definition>
        <argsstring></argsstring>
        <name>vlsn</name>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Consistent read view LSN. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Originally read-only transactions receive a read view lsn upon creation and do not see further changes. Other transactions are expected to be read-write and have vlsn == INT64_MAX to read newest data. Once a value read by such a transaction (T) is overwritten by another commiting transaction, T permanently goes to read view that does not see this change. If T does not have any write statements by the commit time it will be committed successfully, or aborted as conflicted otherwise. </para>        </detaileddescription>
